 "notes": "AxionPhoton g_agamma 95% CL limit (Delta chi^2 <= 3.84) on QCD axion/ALP dark matter decaying to two photons, from JWST blank-sky observations (MIRI 0.1-0.5 eV red region + NIRSpec 0.5-4 eV blue region). Headline curve is the lower boundary (deepest excluded coupling) of the combined MIRI+NIRSpec excluded region in Fig. 2, extracted by vector analysis of Plots/limits_miri+nirspec_v5.pdf (drawings 2=red MIRI fill, 3=blue NIRSpec fill). Log-log axes calibrated from tick marks: x 0.1-4 eV (487.6 px/decade), y 1e-13..1e-9 GeV^-1 (83.2 px/decade). Curve is highly spiky (per-wavelength spectral limits); reported points are the lower envelope binned in log-mass. Limit is a decay signal depending on the D-factor (NFW column density, rs=24 kpc, rho_s=0.18 GeV/cm^3) rather than a single local density, so dm_density_assumed is null; assumes axions are 100% of DM. No ancillary data file in e-print.",
